## Limits and output boundary

No Node or Android implementation audit, product DB/raw private rollout mutation, real-source replay, live server, device/model operation, permanent new test, full Rust/vendor suite, journal write, Git mutation or task closure occurred. Tests may create their own isolated temporary fixtures and build artifacts under the existing workflow. Only this report and safe `rust-audit.json` were authored as review outputs. Current source identity/checkpoint/cut/capability protection was checked; exhaustive multi-level branch/resend, huge inputs, all external host variants and unrequested end-to-end matrices were not run.

H1 consumer merge/product persistence and S5/S6 business acceptance must be assessed by their owning reviewers. Existing B/Q budget failures, old connection error text, registration candidate and management association gaps are neither deleted nor converted to Rust findings or resolved claims by this report.

`next_route: null` — this delegated read-only scope produced no Rust repair request; the parent review owns the cumulative verdict and any user-authorized follow-up.
